{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1106","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Lunar New Year and a Recursive Sequence"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Lunar New Year is approaching, and Bob received a gift from his friend recently — a recursive sequence!"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" He loves this sequence very much and wants to play with it."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let $$$f_1, f_2, \\ldots, f_i, \\ldots$$$ be an infinite sequence of positive integers. Bob knows that for $$$i \\gt k$$$, $$$f_i$$$ can be obtained by the following recursive equation:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$$$$f_i = \\left(f_{i - 1} ^ {b_1} \\cdot f_{i - 2} ^ {b_2} \\cdot \\cdots \\cdot f_{i - k} ^ {b_k}\\right) \\bmod p,$$$$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"which in short is"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$$$$f_i = \\left(\\prod_{j = 1}^{k} f_{i - j}^{b_j}\\right) \\bmod p,$$$$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"where $$$p = 998\\,244\\,353$$$ (a widely-used prime), $$$b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_k$$$ are known integer constants, and $$$x \\bmod y$$$ denotes the remainder of $$$x$$$ divided by $$$y$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Bob lost the values of $$$f_1, f_2, \\ldots, f_k$$$, which is extremely troublesome – these are the basis of the sequence! Luckily, Bob remembers the first $$$k - 1$$$ elements of the sequence: $$$f_1 = f_2 = \\ldots = f_{k - 1} = 1$$$ and the $$$n$$$-th element: $$$f_n = m$$$. Please find any possible value of $$$f_k$$$. If no solution exists, just tell Bob that it is impossible to recover his favorite sequence, regardless of Bob's sadness."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a positive integer $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\leq k \\leq 100$$$), denoting the length of the sequence $$$b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_k$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$k$$$ positive integers $$$b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_k$$$ ($$$1 \\leq b_i \\lt p$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line contains two positive integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$k \\lt n \\leq 10^9$$$, $$$1 \\leq m \\lt p$$$), which implies $$$f_n = m$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output a possible value of $$$f_k$$$, where $$$f_k$$$ is a positive integer satisfying $$$1 \\leq f_k \\lt p$$$. If there are multiple answers, print any of them. If no such $$$f_k$$$ makes $$$f_n = m$$$, output $$$-1$$$ instead."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is easy to show that if there are some possible values of $$$f_k$$$, there must be at least one satisfying $$$1 \\leq f_k \\lt p$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n2 3 5\n4 16\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n4 7 1 5 6\n7 14187219\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n8\n2 3 5 6 1 7 9 10\n23333 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n2\n88888 66666\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n-1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n998244352 998244352 998244352\n4 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n-1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n10\n283 463 213 777 346 201 463 283 102 999\n2333333 6263423\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n382480067\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample, we have $$$f_4 = f_3^2 \\cdot f_2^3 \\cdot f_1^5$$$. Therefore, applying $$$f_3 = 4$$$, we have $$$f_4 = 16$$$. Note that there can be multiple answers."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third sample, applying $$$f_7 = 1$$$ makes $$$f_{23333} = 1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fourth sample, no such $$$f_1$$$ makes $$$f_{88888} = 66666$$$. Therefore, we output $$$-1$$$ instead."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1106F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1106/problem/F"}